"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/KComponents","kind":"symbol","title":"KComponents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k-components of an undirected graph (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k ≥ 1,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the maximal sets of vertices whose induced subgraph is k-vertex-connected, that is, has more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than k vertices and stays connected after removing any k − 1 of them. The 1-components are the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connected components with an edge, the 2-components the blocks of three or more vertices; every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"k-component lies inside a (k − 1)-component. Components at one level may share fewer than k"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices."}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/kcomponents","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KComponents"}]},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/ComplementView/kComponents()":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/complementview\/kcomponents()","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/ComplementView\/kComponents()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity11KComponentsV","text":"KComponents","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"title":"kComponents()"},"doc://GraphOperations/documentation/GraphOperations/ComplementView":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The complement of a graph, as a lazy view. Made by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"complement